From 51f08bea2c16c4b2025b8fa4b6ac55f699a47786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] power: supply: read-only SM5703 fuel gauge driver

The SM-T715's battery gauge (SM5703 fuel gauge block, I2C 0x71) exposed
as a power_supply: capacity, voltage, OCV, current, temperature and a
status derived from the current sign.  The driver never writes the chip:
the battery model, calibration and alarms stay as Android's driver set
them, and regmap only allows reading the registers decoded here (the
interrupt status register is cleared on read, so it is excluded).  It
polls every 30 s and reports changes.

Checked on the SM-T715: 99 %, 4.35 V, -94 mA on battery, 38.9 C,
"Discharging", FG_OP_STATUS low byte 0x07 (model loaded), and UPower
lists the battery.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
